    <!--
        Dedicated monochrome/themed-icon layer for the adaptive icon — a simple, bold
        star, NOT the full star+hammer+keyboard foreground artwork. Android's themed-icon
        generator (used for notification badges, Material You themed icons) can't cleanly
        derive a silhouette from the full detailed artwork and falls back to a smooth blur
        instead of a legible shape — this happens regardless of source resolution, since
        it's the OS's own monochrome-synthesis step, not a scaling artifact. Keep this
        simple; the detailed illustration stays in <foreground>/<background> for the
        actual launcher icon, unaffected. See ExplainReceiver.kt operational_notes.
    -->
